Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CyclicHochschildDifferential", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"fd831637-a214-43c5-af3c-795be202a46d"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CyclicHochschildDifferential"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CyclicHochschildDifferential", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9ab6adc9-894a-45c3-8b5c-5da8b925d50f"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the differential of the cyclic word ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", induced letter by letter by the differential of the Poincare duality \
algebra that ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " carries.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"fd9c17c6-5034-4c3d-9452-1ccb788041f8"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CyclicHochschildDifferential"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CyclicHochschildDifferential", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["pairing", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b5175885-b518-4097-8b49-d881c5422027"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the extension of the differential as a derivation, applied to a \
product ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " of cyclic words."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"7bfe3f44-708b-4d15-bbfc-bb0696c6859f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is the operation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d62c29b6-181a-416c-bb44-9140c732b8a4"],
 " of the dIBL structure of a cyclic cochain complex. It takes one cyclic \
word to a sum of cyclic words of the same length."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the differential is read from the \
\"Algebra\" key that GradedPairing[algebra] attaches, and from nothing else, \
so the alphabet is data: a pairing built by hand from degrees and values \
carries no algebra and every word is closed, with no message; no alternative \
was recorded. The sign is the running sign of the letters after the replaced \
one. It is the prefix rule of the literature read through the reversal sign \
$(-1)^{\\sum_{r<s}\\eta_r\\eta_s}$ that relates the cyclic words to the \
functionals of the literature; both give the same operation in different \
coordinates, and the sign is pinned by the Leibniz rule, as the statement \
that the differential kills the canonical Maurer-Cartan element. The function \
takes no \"EmptyWord\" option. Alternative name considered: \
CyclicDifferential, the name until 2026-09-30. Prior art: the Wolfram \
Language has no cyclic Hochschild complex; the verification suites pin the \
function on the two nilmanifold alphabets against their differential \
pairings, and check that it squares to zero, lowers the degree, anticommutes \
with the bracket and the co-bracket, and vanishes on an alphabet of the \
catalogue exactly when its quotient carries the differential 0.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->137278674,ExpressionUUID->"a73bc372-9bf4-4a8a-9a21-de420d968278"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each letter in turn is replaced by its image under the differential dual to \
the one of the algebra, with the sign ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "301dda64-0a58-403b-bff5-d8ea4f7a6050"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ad7658c0-5ad6-4819-82e4-1920358cb7e4"],
 " being the bar degree of the letters after it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"01e47aaf-8dd8-4b7e-bef9-21069145d1cc"],

Cell["\<\
It lowers the degree by one, and it preserves the length of a word and the \
number of factors of a product.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7e309845-0a9a-4d58-9056-7db12edd1366"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is read from the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Algebra\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "370d3720-41f3-465e-89d2-4c0b2011ed6a"],
 " key of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 ", which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["GradedPairing"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/GradedPairing", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["algebra", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1ab88f06-6eb6-4c2d-bf47-3eb31a4f9f1b"],
 " attaches, for instance to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"GradedPairing", "[", 
   RowBox[{"NondegenerateQuotient", "[", "model", "]"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7fc8f3c7-6241-4fa4-94c1-1c12c3f86cb8"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1348ca82-e1d5-44cc-bf08-95fa0de3b999"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A pairing built from degrees and pairing values carries no algebra, and the \
differential of every word is then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8fb6dac7-26d5-447d-9c27-cdd03153cda0"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d5cf2979-5e8b-4e8b-bb6d-bd61b836331f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is also ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1107bf8f-88a6-467b-be42-949f38f24af1"],
 " when the Poincare duality algebra carries the differential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4436d341-4a7b-4966-b8bb-70e5d628d555"],
 ", as the nondegenerate quotient of a formal model does. The alphabets of \
the non-formal models ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<HeisenbergNilmanifold\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ba3af5db-8cae-43fc-af7c-dd635d7a5ae1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<KodairaThurston\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "84c05ea8-dd11-4295-bcbc-bc5fcc9c0eff"],
 " of the catalogue carry a nonzero differential."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aa86258e-fe3f-4ccc-a148-eb12d5f6f72c"],

Cell["\<\
On a cyclic word the operation carries no degree-shift sign, so it is the \
same in both pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"79421678-e941-46cd-9b62-72b27f96c726"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the second form the differential is applied to each factor of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in turn, with the Koszul sign of the shuffle that brings it to the front. \
The convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " selects the picture of the product."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"43dbff8a-39b9-4009-9313-b99ff6ba8ee3"],

Cell["\<\
Both forms are linear: they distribute over sums and pull out scalars.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5c7f5812-39fd-405b-851a-b3d99377e774"],

Cell["A word may be given as the list of its letters.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c4295f3b-3f2d-4137-8702-8c670d5e876c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A product whose head disagrees with the convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " returns unevaluated."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1d945d65-6160-4ad9-aed3-bb1eb363e85c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The differential is the first summand of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalBeilinsonDrinfeldOperator"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalBeilinsonDrinfeldOperator", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "95e5ff2d-9d06-4216-8af2-3db9504a3962"],
 " and of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TwistedDifferential"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/TwistedDifferential", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "38e8a3b6-5570-43f2-9174-ca8896aba7c0"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"06984f1c-28a8-4678-b284-1f9cca351c48"]
}, Open  ]],

